/* The sign on each house cusp for the house pages (houses 2, 4, 7 and 10 use the sign pages' own sections), written about you (see CLAUDE.md). */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.houseCusps = {
  "1": {
    "aries": "With Aries rising, you arrive before you have quite finished deciding to come. People meet your energy first: the quick stride, the direct gaze, the way you say what you think within five minutes of being introduced. Your body likes to move and runs hot, and you are usually the first on your feet when something needs doing. Starting things is effortless, so you sign up, volunteer and lead the charge while others are still reading the instructions. This openness makes you easy to trust, because nothing is hidden behind your face. Impatience is the cost, and a flash of temper or a half-finished project can leave a sharper impression than you intended. Life keeps rewarding you for being brave in plain sight.",
    "taurus": "Taurus rising gives you a calm, grounded presence that people notice before you speak. You enter a room without hurry, take the comfortable chair, and somehow the atmosphere settles around you. Your body matters to you in a physical, sensual way: good fabric against your skin, a proper meal, a long walk that leaves your legs pleasantly tired. Strangers read you as steady and kind, the person they would trust to mind their bag while they nip to the loo. New beginnings take you a while, since you want to know the ground is solid before you put your weight on it. Once you commit, you keep going long after the enthusiasts have drifted off. The same stubbornness that makes you reliable also makes you very hard to shift when change is overdue.",
    "gemini": "Your first impression is quick, curious and chatty, because Gemini rising puts your mind right at the front door. Within minutes of meeting someone you have asked three questions, made a joke and found out where they grew up. Your body is restless: fidgeting hands, a phone always within reach, a face that changes expression halfway through a sentence. For years people guess you are younger than you are, and a youthful lightness stays with you. Starting things is easy and exciting, and you often begin several at once, drawn to whatever is newest. People can mistake your brightness for a lack of depth, and sometimes you let them, because it is easier than explaining. Underneath all the talk sits a real hunger to understand everything you meet.",
    "cancer": "Cancer rising gives you a soft, watchful way of meeting the world. You read a room before stepping fully into it, noticing who looks tired, who is upset, who needs a cup of tea. People warm to you quickly and often tell you things on first meeting that they had not planned to share with anyone. Your face shows your feelings more than you would like, and your body answers your moods, with a stomach that knots under stress and energy that ebbs and flows with your emotions. New ventures begin cautiously, tested for safety before you commit. When you feel judged, a protective shell goes up so fast that strangers mistake it for coolness. Once you feel at home somewhere, your care quietly fills the whole space.",
    "leo": "People notice you when you walk in, and with Leo rising that is rarely an accident. You carry yourself with warmth and a sense of occasion: the good coat, hair that has been thought about, the big hug for a friend you have not seen in weeks. Your body language is open and generous, and you visibly light up when someone is paying attention. Starting things comes naturally whenever you can put your heart and your name to them. Others feel included around you, as if the party improved the moment they arrived. Pride is the tender spot, and a cool reception or a careless comment about how you look can sting for days. Being truly seen is how you come alive, and you hand that same attention back to everyone in the room.",
    "virgo": "With Virgo rising, you come across as composed, observant and quietly capable. You clock the crooked picture frame and the typo on the menu within moments of arriving, even if you keep it to yourself. Your body is finely tuned to what you eat, how you sleep and how much is on your plate, and you feel slightly off long before anyone else would notice. People bring you their problems because you look like someone who knows how things work. New projects start with a list and a sensible plan rather than a leap in the dark. Self-criticism is the hidden weight you carry, judging your own appearance and performance far more harshly than anyone around you does. Your modest, useful presence earns a kind of trust that louder people never quite manage.",
    "libra": "Libra rising gives you an easy charm that smooths the first moments of any meeting. You smile readily, find the thing you have in common, and leave people feeling pleasant in your company. Appearance matters to you as a form of courtesy: a well chosen outfit, a tidy room, a graceful way of moving through a crowded bar. Most things begin better for you with a partner or at least a sounding board, and decisions can drag while you weigh every side. Friends send you in to calm an argument because you seem so fair. Keeping the peace can cost you your own opinion, and people come away liking you without really knowing what you think. Beneath the polish lives a genuine love of harmony and beauty that shapes every choice you make.",
    "scorpio": "Scorpio rising gives you a presence people feel before they understand it. Your gaze is steady and searching, and strangers sometimes find themselves confessing things to you within the hour. You give away very little at first, preferring to watch and work out who is safe before you reveal anything real. Your body holds intensity: a strong constitution, a powerful stillness, and energy that burns through you when a feeling goes unspoken. Starting something new is an all or nothing decision, and once you are in, you go deep. Some people read your privacy as suspicion, and you can guard yourself so well that warmth struggles to get through the door. More than once in your life you shed an old version of yourself and come back stronger.",
    "sagittarius": "You meet life with the door open and a bag half packed, which is how Sagittarius rising shows itself. People see someone friendly, frank and optimistic, quick to laugh and quicker to say exactly what they think. Your body wants space and movement: long walks, a sport, a spontaneous trip booked because the flights were cheap on a Tuesday. You start things with huge enthusiasm and a sense that it will all work out, which surprisingly often it does. Honesty is part of your charm, though a blunt remark can land harder than you meant it to. Restlessness pulls you onward before some things are finished, and the people who wanted you to stay feel left on the platform. An appetite for meaning turns every stage of your life into another journey.",
    "capricorn": "Capricorn rising gives you a serious, capable first impression, older than your years when you are young and younger than your years later on. People assume you are in charge, even when you are simply standing in the queue. You hold yourself with reserve, measuring a room and deciding how much of yourself it has earned. Your body responds well to effort and discipline, and you push through tiredness rather than admit to it. New beginnings are strategic, planned three steps ahead before the first is taken. Responsibility settles on your shoulders early, and lightness can feel like something you have to deserve first. Those who take the time to know you discover a dry wit and a loyalty that never wavers.",
    "aquarius": "Aquarius rising makes you instantly a little different from everyone else in the room. Sometimes it is the clothes, sometimes the unexpected opinion, or the way you chat to the waiter as if he were an old friend. People find you friendly yet hard to pin down, open to everyone yet oddly detached. Your body runs on a kind of nervous electricity, with bursts of energy and strange sleeping hours whenever an idea grips you. You start things by asking why they are normally done that way and then inventing your own method. Independence matters so much that closeness can feel like pressure, and others sometimes sense they are being held at arm's length. Around you, people feel allowed to be odd, and that permission is a quiet kind of gift.",
    "pisces": "Pisces rising gives you a soft, dreamy presence that people find easy to project onto. Strangers tell you their troubles in the supermarket queue, and friends say you understand them without being told. Your body is highly sensitive to atmosphere, crowds and substances, and you soak up the mood of a room as if it were your own. New beginnings happen by drifting rather than marching, following a feeling more than a plan. Kindness and imagination make you gentle company and a natural artist. Boundaries are the hard part: you blur into whatever others need you to be and lose track of your own shape. Solitude, music and time near water bring you back to yourself every single time."
  },
  "3": {
    "aries": "Your mind moves fast, and you say what you think the moment you think it. With Aries on this cusp, conversation is a lively sport: you interrupt, you debate, and a good argument pleases you more than a polite chat ever could. Learning happens by diving in, skimming the instructions and working out the rest as you go. Brothers, sisters and neighbours know you as the direct one, and your early family life probably held some competitive rivalry. Messages get answered within seconds, and your emails are short enough to seem curt. Snap judgements cause most of your trouble, since you can wound someone before you notice you have spoken. Courage in speech is your strength, and you say out loud what others are too nervous to say.",
    "taurus": "Taurus on the cusp of your third house gives you a steady, practical mind that likes to take its time. You think things through properly and would rather understand one idea well than skim ten. Your voice is often pleasant and calm, and people find the way you explain things reassuring. Learning works best through the hands and senses: doing, touching, repeating until it sticks for good. With siblings and neighbours you are the dependable one, still in touch with friends from the street where you grew up. Once your mind is made up it stays made up, and new information can struggle to find a way in. Plain common sense lets you cut through noise that leaves quicker minds in a flap.",
    "gemini": "Gemini on this cusp makes your mind a busy crossroads of messages, ideas and chatter. You are the one with seven tabs open, three group chats buzzing and a podcast playing in the background. Words come easily, whether you are texting, telling a story or explaining the route to a stranger on a train. Siblings, cousins and neighbours play a large part in your life, and you know half the street by name. Learning is a joy as long as it stays varied, and you pick up facts, phrases and skills at remarkable speed. Scattered attention is the price: you know a little about everything and can struggle to finish the book on your bedside table. Curiosity keeps your mind young for your whole life.",
    "cancer": "With Cancer here, feeling colours every thought, and you remember conversations by how they made you feel. You speak with warmth and reach for a personal story sooner than an abstract point. Ties with brothers, sisters and cousins run deep, carrying old loyalties and a few old hurts. You learn best in a safe, friendly setting, and a cold teacher can shut your mind down entirely. Your neighbourhood feels like an extended home, and you notice the day the corner shop changes hands. Moods sway your judgement, and a remark said in the wrong tone can replay in your head for days. Memory and empathy give your words a power to touch people that cleverness alone never has.",
    "leo": "You talk with flair, and Leo on this cusp puts real warmth and drama into everything you say. A story told by you comes with gestures, voices and a perfectly timed pause before the punchline. You enjoy being heard and often end up as the group's spokesperson, the one who presents the idea or stands up for the toast. Learning thrives on praise and encouragement and wilts when you feel overlooked. With siblings there can be friendly rivalry over who gets the attention, alongside fierce loyalty. Admitting you got a fact wrong comes hard, and you can take over a conversation without realising it. When you speak from the heart, the whole table leans in.",
    "virgo": "Virgo on this cusp gives you a precise, analytical mind that misses nothing. You spot the error in the spreadsheet, the flaw in the argument and the stray apostrophe on the greengrocer's sign. Your speech is careful and useful, and you like to check your facts before you share them. Learning comes through method: notes, lists, highlighted pages and practice until it is right. Siblings and neighbours call on you to fill in a form or untangle a practical problem. Worry is the downside, with an overactive mind that keeps you awake at night running through everything that could go wrong. Complicated things become simple once they have passed through your head, and people love you for it.",
    "libra": "Your mind looks for balance, and with Libra here you naturally see both sides of any argument. You speak gracefully, choose your words with care, and have a knack for saying hard things kindly. Conversation is one of your great pleasures, especially one to one over a long coffee, where ideas can bounce back and forth. Relationships with siblings and neighbours tend to be pleasant, and you are the one who smooths over the family squabble at Christmas. Learning goes best with a study partner or a lively discussion. Indecision is the snag: you weigh the options for so long that someone else chooses, or you agree simply to avoid friction. People trust your judgement precisely because it is so evidently fair.",
    "scorpio": "Scorpio on this cusp gives your mind depth, focus and a detective's instinct. You read between the lines of every message and notice what someone carefully left unsaid. Small talk bores you, and one honest conversation about something real beats an evening of pleasantries. A subject that grips you becomes an obsession, and you research it until you hit the bottom. Ties with siblings can be intense, holding secrets, strong loyalty or old power struggles. In anger your words know exactly where to aim, and the damage can last for years. That same penetrating mind makes you a formidable researcher, listener or writer, able to reach the truth others miss.",
    "sagittarius": "With Sagittarius here, your mind is broad, enthusiastic and always reaching for the bigger picture. You love a conversation that wanders from gossip to philosophy to holiday plans in the same half hour. Learning excites you when it opens a new horizon, and you collect languages, courses and books from every corner of the world. You speak frankly and with humour, and people enjoy your stories even when you exaggerate them. Siblings and neighbours can be scattered far and wide, or you were the one who moved away. Details bore you and you skip the small print, which lands you in avoidable muddles. Your enthusiasm for ideas makes you a natural teacher who sets other minds alight.",
    "capricorn": "Capricorn on this cusp gives you a serious, structured mind that values facts and results. You think before you speak and see little point in wasting words on gossip. Learning comes through steady effort, and you are the one who reads the manual and passes the exam through sheer discipline. Your communication is concise, practical and often very drily funny. Early life can have brought responsibility for a younger sibling, or a sense that you had to grow up quickly. Secret doubts about your own intelligence can keep you silent rather than risk sounding foolish. Over the years your mind becomes a real authority, and people seek out your well considered view.",
    "aquarius": "Your mind works in leaps and flashes, and Aquarius on this cusp makes you a genuinely original thinker. You notice patterns others miss and enjoy ideas that turn the usual view upside down. Conversation with you veers towards technology, social questions, science and the future. Learning goes best when you are free to follow your own route, and rigid teaching makes you tune out or rebel. Siblings and neighbours feel more like friends, or the bond with them is unusual in some way. You prize open minds yet hold your own conclusions with surprising stubbornness, which catches people off guard. Problems others considered settled get fresh solutions once you start tinkering with them.",
    "pisces": "Pisces on this cusp gives you an imaginative, intuitive mind that thinks in images and feelings. You pick up the mood of a conversation before you catch its words, and you often know what someone means before they finish. Learning happens by absorption: music, stories, pictures and quiet daydreaming by the window rather than drills. Your speech is gentle and poetic, and facts can slip through your fingers like water. With siblings there is often a strong, wordless bond, or a sense of looking after someone vulnerable. Clarity is hard won, since you drift, forget appointments or tell people what they want to hear. What cannot easily be put into words is exactly what you are able to express."
  },
  "5": {
    "aries": "Joy arrives for you in bursts of action, and Aries on this cusp keeps your pleasures lively. You love a challenge, a game you can win, a dare you cannot resist, a weekend away booked on impulse at midnight. Romance starts fast and hot, with you making the first move and relishing the chase. Creativity flows through bold, spontaneous work: the canvas attacked in one sitting, the song written in twenty minutes. With children, yours or other people's, you are the one who starts the pillow fight and races them to the park gate. Boredom sets in quickly once the thrill fades, and a hobby or a crush can be dropped as fast as it was picked up. Being around you makes life feel like an adventure.",
    "taurus": "Taurus on this cusp makes your joy slow, sensual and deeply physical. Pleasure means a long lunch, a garden in full bloom, a favourite album played on a proper speaker. Romance unfolds at an unhurried pace, built on touch, loyalty and small comforts rather than fireworks. Creativity comes through the hands: baking, pottery, singing, anything with texture and beauty you can hold. With children you offer steadiness, cuddles and a well stocked biscuit tin. Indulgence is the snag, and you can settle so comfortably into familiar pleasures that nothing new gets a look in. Your talent for savouring life teaches the people around you how to slow down and enjoy it.",
    "gemini": "With Gemini here, fun lives in words, ideas and variety. You love quizzes, word games, clever films, witty banter across a dinner table and a new hobby every few months. Romance begins in conversation, and you fall for minds before bodies, sometimes over a single brilliant text message. Creatively you are drawn to writing, podcasts, comedy or anything with a quick turnaround. With children you are playful and chatty, the grown up who invents bedtime stories and happily answers the fortieth question. Restlessness makes it hard to stay with one love or one project, and you can flirt your way out of anything that gets too deep. Lightness and curiosity keep your heart young for life.",
    "cancer": "Joy for you is bound up with home, family and feeling safe, and Cancer on this cusp makes pleasure a tender thing. Your happiest moments are often at your own table, cooking for people you love, or curled under a blanket watching a film you have seen twenty times. Romance needs emotional safety before it can bloom, and once you trust someone you care for them deeply. Creativity draws on memory and feeling, producing work that is nostalgic, personal and moving. Children, yours or the ones you nurture, sit close to your heart, and you protect them almost to a fault. Hurt feelings can send you into your shell to sulk rather than play. Every celebration you host feels like a homecoming.",
    "leo": "Leo on this cusp puts your heart centre stage, and joy for you is bright, generous and expressive. You love to perform, host, dress up and throw a party people talk about for months. Romance is grand and theatrical, full of gestures and declarations, and you want to be adored in return. Creative work is where you feel most alive, and you pour pride and love into whatever you make, from a birthday cake to a stage role. Children light you up, and you are a warm, encouraging presence in their lives. Needing applause is the soft spot, and a lukewarm response to your work or your love can flatten you. Your big heart makes everyone near you feel special.",
    "virgo": "Virgo on this cusp makes your pleasures careful, skilful and quietly satisfying. Joy often comes from getting something exactly right: a perfect sourdough, a finished thousand-piece jigsaw, a vegetable patch without a single weed. Romance grows through small acts of service, and you show love by remembering how someone takes their tea. Creativity thrives on craft and technique, and you polish a piece until it meets your exacting standards. With children you are attentive and practical, sitting beside them for homework and making sure they eat something green. Perfectionism can steal the fun, because you judge your own efforts too harshly to relax into play. Work made by your hands carries real quality and care.",
    "libra": "With Libra here, joy is about beauty, company and harmony. You love galleries, well designed spaces, music, dancing and an evening spent with someone lovely across a candlelit table. Romance sits at the centre of your happiness, and you enjoy courtship, charm and the pleasure of being part of a couple. Creative expression leans towards balance and elegance, whether in fashion, design, music or words. With children you are fair and gentle, teaching manners and kindness by example. Relying on a partner for your fun can leave you unsure what you enjoy on your own. Every pleasure becomes lovelier once you have added your touch of grace.",
    "scorpio": "Scorpio on this cusp makes joy intense, private and all-consuming. Casual fun holds little appeal; you want experiences that move you to the core, from a gripping thriller read in one night to a love affair that changes you. Romance is passionate and loyal, charged with strong desire and a need for complete trust. Creativity explores dark or hidden themes, and making something can feel like a transformation for you and for anyone who sees it. With children you are fiercely protective and emotionally attuned. Jealousy and possessiveness are the traps, and a romance can turn into a power struggle when trust wavers. Play, for you, always reaches down into something profound.",
    "sagittarius": "With Sagittarius on this cusp, joy lives in freedom, adventure and laughter. You love travel, sport, big ideas and anything that pushes your horizons a little further. Romance thrives with a fellow explorer, and you often fall for people from other cultures or very different backgrounds. Creativity flows when it tells a story or carries a belief, and you enjoy writing, teaching or performing with humour. With children you are the fun adult who takes them camping and answers the big questions honestly. Commitment can feel like a cage, and you wander off when a romance or project starts to feel routine. Your optimism turns ordinary Saturdays into occasions.",
    "capricorn": "Capricorn on this cusp makes joy something you earn and build over time. You take your pleasures seriously, whether that means a hobby you master, a marathon you train for or a creative project with a clear goal. Romance is cautious at first, and you would rather have a partner with maturity and substance than a fleeting fling. Creativity comes through discipline and structure, and your work improves steadily with age. With children you are responsible and supportive, the parent who turns up to every match, though the role can feel very serious. Playing without purpose is the hard part, and fun easily gets postponed until the work is done. Life grows lighter and more playful for you the older you get.",
    "aquarius": "Joy for you is unconventional, and Aquarius on this cusp gives your pleasures an unusual twist. You enjoy science, gadgets, group activities, festivals and anything that brings friends together around an idea. Romance often starts as friendship, and you need a partner who respects your independence and your odd hours. Creatively you experiment, drawn to new media, strange ideas and styles that break the rules. With children you treat them as individuals and actively encourage their quirks. Lovers can feel you keep your heart at a slight distance, as if part of you is always watching from outside. Everything you create feels fresh and faintly ahead of its time.",
    "pisces": "Pisces on this cusp makes joy dreamy, romantic and deeply imaginative. You love music, film, the sea, poetry and anything that lets you slip away from ordinary life for a while. Romance can be idealistic, and you fall for the fantasy of a person before you meet the real one. Creativity flows easily through art, music, dance or photography, and inspiration seems to come from somewhere beyond you. With children you are gentle, intuitive and compassionate, at home in their inner worlds. Pleasure can slide into escapism, and disappointment follows when reality fails to match the dream. Magic follows you into everything you love."
  },
  "6": {
    "aries": "You attack the working day, and Aries on this cusp means you like to get straight into action. Mornings start at speed: a quick coffee, a hard workout, then straight at the task list. Independence, challenge and a bit of competition bring out your best, while slow colleagues drive you to distraction. Your body thrives on vigorous movement, and without exercise you turn restless and irritable. Health tendencies lean towards heat and haste, with tension headaches, small knocks and burnout from pushing too hard. Routine loses its grip on you the moment it becomes dull, so habits start strong and fade. On any team you are the one who gets things started and gets them done.",
    "taurus": "Taurus on this cusp gives you a steady, reliable way through the working day. You like a set routine, a comfortable chair, the same lunch spot, and you hate being rushed by anyone. Your work is patient and produces solid results that last. Your body likes regular meals, good sleep and gentle movement such as walking or gardening, and it responds beautifully to consistency. The throat and neck carry your tension, and rich food and comfortable habits can creep up on you. Resistance to change can keep you in a job or routine long after it has stopped serving you. Everyone relies on you to keep things running, and you rarely let them down.",
    "gemini": "With Gemini here, your working day is full of variety, conversation and juggling. You thrive in a job with emails, calls, meetings and a dozen different tasks, and a dull routine drains you within weeks. Colleagues know you as the one with the information, a quick answer and a joke by the kettle. Your body is sensitive to nervous strain, and too much screen time leaves you wired yet exhausted. Breathing, hands and nerves need looking after, and short walks between tasks help your mind settle. Scattered focus makes it hard to finish things, and you spread yourself thin across too many jobs. Almost any workplace can use a mind as adaptable as yours.",
    "cancer": "Cancer on this cusp brings care and feeling into your daily work. You want a workplace that feels like a family, with colleagues who look out for each other. You are the one who remembers birthdays, brings in cake and notices when someone has been crying in the toilets. Your wellbeing is closely tied to your emotions, and stress often shows up in your stomach or digestion first. Homely routines, such as cooking your own lunch or a quiet evening ritual, keep you balanced. Criticism at work feels personal, and a bad day can leave you moody for the rest of the week. Wherever people need looking after, you do some of your finest work.",
    "leo": "Leo on this cusp means you want to shine in your everyday work. You take pride in doing a job well and glow when your boss or team notices. Roles involving leadership, creativity or performance suit you, and you bring warmth and loyalty to any workplace. Your vitality depends on joy, and a job without heart drains your energy faster than long hours ever could. The heart and back are areas to look after, and exercise you genuinely enjoy, such as dancing, keeps you strong. Pride can make humble tasks or correction hard to accept. Your enthusiasm lifts the morale of everyone you work alongside.",
    "virgo": "Virgo on this cusp is right at home, making you efficient, precise and devoted to doing things properly. You love a well organised day, a colour coded calendar and a desk with everything in its place. Colleagues rely on you for accuracy and practical help, and you notice the problems nobody else has spotted. Your body is sensitive to diet and stress, and you usually know exactly which foods agree with you. Digestion and nervous tension carry your worries, which tend to show up physically. Perfectionism and overwork pull you down, since you take on too much and nothing ever feels quite good enough. Any team functions better with your skill and service in it.",
    "libra": "With Libra here, harmony in your working life matters a great deal. You work best in a pleasant environment with cooperative colleagues, and conflict or ugliness at work genuinely unsettles you. You are diplomatic and fair, often the person mediating disputes or bringing a divided team back together. Your health benefits from balance in everything: food, rest, work, and some beauty around you, even just flowers on the desk. The lower back and kidneys are sensitive areas, and disharmony at work affects your wellbeing more than you admit. Putting your own needs first is hard when you are busy accommodating everyone else. Colleagues remember your grace and tact long after they have moved on.",
    "scorpio": "Scorpio on this cusp brings intensity and focus to your daily work. You throw yourself into tasks with determination and work long hours on anything that grips you. Depth suits you better than breadth, and you excel at research, investigation or problems everyone else avoids. Your body has strong powers of recovery but holds stress deeply, and a hard run, a sauna or honest talk releases what builds up. The reproductive system and the gut are areas to look after. Power struggles or secrecy at work can create tension, and you can become controlling with colleagues. Whatever you undertake, your commitment and resilience make you formidable.",
    "sagittarius": "With Sagittarius here, you want your daily work to feel meaningful and free. Routine bores you, and you prefer a job with variety, travel, learning or a strong sense of purpose. You are optimistic and cheerful at work, and colleagues enjoy your humour and your big ideas in meetings. Your body likes activity and fresh air, and your health improves with sport, hiking or anything that gets you outside. Hips, thighs and liver are sensitive areas, and overindulgence catches up with you. Overpromising and ignoring details cause most of your problems at work. You inspire the people you work with, and many of them learn more from you than from any manual.",
    "capricorn": "Capricorn on this cusp makes you a disciplined, hardworking and responsible presence at work. You like structure, clear goals and a plan, and you take your duties very seriously. Colleagues respect your reliability and competence, and you often rise into a position of authority. Your body benefits from routine and steady exercise, though you neglect rest in pursuit of your goals. Bones, joints, teeth and skin are areas to look after. Workaholism is the danger, as you can define yourself by your productivity and struggle to switch off even on holiday. Whatever you build through daily effort is built to last.",
    "aquarius": "With Aquarius here, you need freedom and fresh thinking in your daily work. Rigid routines and micromanagement stifle you, and you do your best work with flexible hours or working from wherever you like. Technology, science and social causes appeal to you, and you bring new ideas to every workplace. Your body is sensitive to nervous tension and irregular hours, and unconventional approaches to health often suit you best. Circulation and ankles are sensitive areas. Rebelling against pointless rules or holding colleagues at a distance can create friction. When something at work is broken, you are the one who invents a better way.",
    "pisces": "Pisces on this cusp brings compassion and intuition into your daily work. You are drawn to caring, healing or creative work, and you want your job to help others in some way. You absorb the moods of colleagues and can come home from a tense office utterly drained. Your body is sensitive to atmosphere, substances and stress, and rest, water and quiet restore you. Feet and immunity are sensitive areas. Lack of structure makes routines hard to keep, and you lose track of time. Kindness and imagination make you gifted as a healer or an artist."
  },
  "8": {
    "aries": "You meet the deep end of life head on. When a crisis lands, a sudden bill, a diagnosis in the family, a breakup that splits the flat, you are the one who acts first and feels later. Desire is direct and urgent for you, and you would rather say what you want in bed than drop hints. Shared money makes you impatient: you hate waiting on a partner's signature or a slow probate, and you have been known to pay off a debt in one furious lump just to be free of it. Transformation comes to you through confrontation, a row that clears the air or a decision made overnight. The cost is that you sometimes burn a bridge you still needed, and the grief catches up with you weeks later.",
    "taurus": "Intimacy for you is built slowly and held tightly. You need to trust someone's body and their bank balance before you let either near yours, and once you do, you are loyal and deeply sensual. Joint accounts, mortgages and inheritances matter to you more than you admit; you remember exactly who paid for what, and you feel a quiet security when shared money is solid. You are the one who keeps a grandmother's ring or the family furniture long after everyone else has moved on. Crisis unsettles you because it threatens what you have built, so your first instinct is to hold still and refuse to budge. That steadiness carries others through upheaval. Letting go of what has already ended is where your real transformation begins, and it rarely comes quickly.",
    "gemini": "You process the heavy things by talking them through. When life turns upside down, you research, you read every forum, you phone three friends and piece together a story that makes sense of it. Desire starts in your head: a clever message, a whispered line, a curiosity about what someone is really like beneath the surface. Shared money tends to be complicated rather than dramatic, with several accounts, a side deal with a sibling or a spreadsheet only you understand. You can talk about death, sex and debt more lightly than most people, which puts others at ease. The trouble is that words become a way to stay safely above feeling, analysing a loss instead of letting it land. Change reaches you properly once you stop explaining it and let yourself be moved.",
    "cancer": "Your deepest bonds feel like family, and you give yourself to them with your whole heart. Intimacy needs emotional safety first; you open up in the dark, after the long talk, when you know you will not be laughed at. Inheritance for you is as much emotional as financial: the recipes, the old grudges, the house you grew up in and what happened there. You look after shared money protectively, squirrelling away a buffer so nobody you love goes without. In a crisis you become the one who brings food, sits by the hospital bed and remembers to feed the cat. Old hurts cling to you, though, and you can carry a family wound for decades as if it were yours to mind. Your transformations tend to come through mourning, and they leave you softer, not harder.",
    "leo": "You want to be wholeheartedly desired, and you bring warmth and drama to the most private corners of your life. In bed you are generous and expressive, and being adored by one person behind closed doors matters more to you than any public applause. Shared money and gifts carry pride: you would rather pay for everyone than feel indebted, and asking for help with a loan stings. When crisis hits, you rise to it with real courage, holding the family together at a funeral or making the phone calls nobody else can face. You come through loss with a stronger sense of who you are. Pride is also what trips you, because admitting you are frightened feels like losing face, so you stage a brave performance while quietly falling apart.",
    "virgo": "You handle the heaviest parts of life by sorting them out. The will is filed, the insurance is up to date, and when someone dies you are the one who closes the accounts and writes the list of who to tell. Debt makes you anxious, so you track shared money carefully and quietly fret when a partner is careless with it. Intimacy grows through small acts of care: remembering what someone likes, noticing when they are tired. You can be shy about desire and critical of your own body, and letting yourself be seen takes time. Crisis sharpens you, because a problem to fix is easier than a feeling to sit with. Real change arrives the day you allow something to stay messy and unfinished, and discover you survive it.",
    "libra": "Your deepest bonds run through partnership, and you want intimacy to feel fair, graceful and mutual. You are attentive in bed and alert to what the other person needs, sometimes more than to what you want yourself. Shared finances go best when both of you put in equally, and an imbalance quietly eats at you even when you say nothing. In a family inheritance you tend to keep the peace, smoothing over squabbles about the house or the jewellery. Crises often arrive through relationships: a divorce, a betrayal, a partner's debts that become yours. You can be diplomatic to the point of swallowing your own anger, and the resentment surfaces later. What transforms you is learning that honest conflict can deepen a bond rather than end it.",
    "scorpio": "This is home territory for you, and you do not flinch from what most people avoid. Intimacy has to be total: you want to know someone's secrets, their fears and their history, and you give your own only once trust is absolute. Sex carries enormous emotional charge, capable of healing you or unsettling you for weeks. You notice where power sits in shared money and guard your own resources closely, sometimes secretively. Crises come in waves across your life, and each one strips something away before you rebuild, stronger and less naive. People bring you their darkest confessions because nothing shocks you. Jealousy and control are the hard part, the urge to hold on tight so you are never betrayed again, and they can suffocate the closeness you crave.",
    "sagittarius": "You bring optimism into places most people find frightening. Even in a crisis you look for the meaning, and a loss often turns into a new philosophy of life or a sudden trip to clear your head. Intimacy for you is adventurous and honest; you want freedom and fun in bed, and heaviness makes you restless. Shared money can come easily, through a generous partner, a lucky inheritance or a deal that pays off, and you are relaxed about it, sometimes too relaxed. You have been known to sign for a loan with a cheerful shrug. Deep emotional intensity can make you want to bolt, so you joke or book a flight rather than stay in the room. A painful truth, allowed to stay, teaches you more than any journey.",
    "capricorn": "You take the serious side of life seriously. Debts get paid, contracts get read, and you are often the one who ends up as executor or the steady hand when the family finances collapse. Trust is earned slowly with you; intimacy builds over years, and you can feel guarded about showing need or desire until you know you are safe. Shared money feels like a responsibility rather than a gift, and you would rather build your own security than depend on anyone. Crisis tends to come through duty, loss or the weight of carrying too much alone. You come through hard times with remarkable endurance, and each one leaves you wiser. What you find hardest is letting someone else carry part of the load, even when they offer.",
    "aquarius": "You approach the intense corners of life with a certain detachment, and that coolness helps you through what flattens others. In a crisis you stay clear headed, working out the practical next step while everyone else panics. Intimacy needs friendship and freedom for you; you want a lover who is also a mate, and possessiveness makes you pull away fast. Your attitudes to sex, money and death are often unconventional, and you are comfortable with arrangements others find strange, from separate finances to open conversations about mortality. Change tends to arrive suddenly: a windfall, a shock, a relationship that ends overnight. The difficulty is emotional distance, since you can intellectualise a loss so thoroughly that you never quite grieve it, and closeness stays one step out of reach.",
    "pisces": "The boundary between you and the people you love dissolves easily, and intimacy for you is close to spiritual. You feel a partner's moods in your own body, and sex can feel like merging rather than meeting. Shared money has a way of slipping through your fingers: you lend without keeping track, forgive debts, or discover later that the paperwork was never quite clear. You are drawn to the mystery of death, dreams and the unseen, and you sit with grieving people with rare gentleness. In a crisis you can rise with compassion or drift into escape, a glass too many, a week in bed. Clear agreements protect your generous heart. Loss changes you through surrender, and you often come out of it more tender and more intuitive than before."
  },
  "9": {
    "aries": "You go after meaning the way you go after anything: fast and first hand. You would rather book the flight tomorrow than plan for a year, and some of your best journeys started with a spontaneous yes. Beliefs for you are things to fight for, and you defend them hotly in the pub, online, or across the family dinner table. Learning grabs you when it is active and challenging, a crash course, a debate, a teacher you can argue with. You are a natural pioneer of ideas, willing to stand up for a cause before it is popular. Impatience shows up as quick judgements and a habit of dropping a subject once the thrill fades. Your outlook grows richest when you let a view you have attacked change you a little.",
    "taurus": "You build your beliefs slowly and hold them for life. Faith for you has to be practical and tested: what works in daily life, what feels true in your body, what has lasted. You travel for pleasure and comfort, returning to the same Italian town or the same beach house rather than chasing the unknown, and you remember every meal. Higher learning suits you when it produces something solid, a qualification, a craft, a skill you can use. Once you have studied a thing properly, you know it thoroughly. Stubbornness is the snag: new ideas can feel like a threat to everything you trust, and you dig in rather than listen. Some of your best growth has come from a journey or a teacher that slowly loosened a conviction you had never questioned.",
    "gemini": "Your curiosity about the world is endless, and your mind travels even when your body stays home. You collect ideas, languages, podcasts and half-read books on philosophy, and you can talk about three belief systems in one breath. Journeys are best when they are varied: several cities, lots of conversations with strangers, a train timetable you enjoy decoding. Learning never really stops for you, and you are often the one who teaches, writes or explains big ideas in simple words. You see every side of an argument, which makes you open minded and fair. The trouble is committing to any single faith or philosophy, and you can end up with lots of fascinating fragments and no centre. One idea that holds you long enough to go deep gives you more than a hundred tasted briefly.",
    "cancer": "Your beliefs are rooted in home, family and feeling. What your parents or grandparents believed shapes you deeply, whether you keep it, soften it, or spend years quietly unpicking it. You travel best with a sense of belonging: visiting relatives abroad, tracing your roots, or finding a foreign town that instantly feels like home. Learning sticks when it moves you emotionally, and you remember the teacher who was kind long after you forget the syllabus. You are protective of the ideas you care about and hurt when they are mocked. Faith for you is a source of comfort in hard times, a place to rest. The difficulty is that your outlook can stay within the familiar, and a different culture touching your heart widens you more than any lecture.",
    "leo": "You want your beliefs to inspire, and you talk about them with warmth and conviction. When you discover a philosophy, a teacher or a cause, you throw yourself into it and often end up leading the study group or giving the talk. Travel for you is a grand adventure: you want the memorable view, the photo that captures it, the story you will tell for years. Learning thrives with encouragement, and a mentor who believed in you shaped more of your life than you realise. You are generous with what you know and love to lift others with it. Pride can make you dogmatic, certain that your way of seeing is the best one. Being a humble student again, happy not to be the expert, is what keeps your wisdom fresh.",
    "virgo": "You look for meaning in the details, and your beliefs have to hold up under careful scrutiny. You read the small print of every philosophy, compare sources and quietly discard what does not add up. Travel works best when it is well organised, with the itinerary checked and the guidebook annotated, though a trip that helps someone, volunteering or a working holiday, satisfies you most. Learning is a lifelong habit, and you are drawn to practical studies: health, craft, analysis, anything that makes you more useful. Faith for you shows up in daily practice rather than grand statements. Your critical eye can tip into scepticism, so that nothing feels quite trustworthy enough to believe. For you, service itself often becomes the truest creed.",
    "libra": "You come to your beliefs through dialogue, weighing different views in search of the fair, balanced truth. People from other cultures fascinate you, and you are often drawn to a partner from somewhere quite different, or you meet someone important while abroad. Travel is best shared, and a beautiful place with good company means more than a solo expedition. Learning appeals when it involves art, law, ethics or relationships, the subtle question of what is right between people. You are a natural diplomat of ideas who can bring opposing camps round one table. The snag is indecision: you can see so many sides that you never quite commit to a view of your own. Your own sense of justice is a sturdier guide than you give it credit for.",
    "scorpio": "You want truth, not comfort, and your beliefs are forged in intensity. Surface religion or easy philosophy leaves you cold; you are drawn to the hidden, the psychological, the taboo, whatever explains why people do what they do. Journeys for you tend to be transformative, and a single trip can change your life, sometimes through an encounter you never talk about. Study grips you when it goes deep: research, psychology, the occult, an obsession you follow for years. Your convictions are fierce, and you rarely hold a view lightly. The risk is that you guard your beliefs so closely that a challenge feels like an attack. Every crisis of faith leaves you with a truer, more hard won understanding of life.",
    "sagittarius": "The wide world is your natural home. You have a hunger for meaning, adventure and horizon, and some of your happiest moments are on the road with no fixed plan. Beliefs matter enormously to you, and you are generous, enthusiastic and funny in the way you share them, whether through teaching, writing or talking late into the night with strangers in a hostel. Higher learning often opens doors for you, and a teacher, a university or a foreign culture has shaped your whole direction. Optimism carries you through, and people find your faith in life contagious. You can preach, though, and assume your truth is everyone's truth, and you promise yourself more adventures than one lifetime can hold. Your outlook deepens once experience humbles it a little.",
    "capricorn": "You take belief and study seriously, and you want your philosophy to be earned, not borrowed. Travel often has a purpose, a conference, a posting abroad, a qualification that needed you to move, and you rarely drift anywhere without a reason. Higher education can come late or with effort, often studying at night while working, and the credentials you gain mean a great deal to you. You respect tradition and the wisdom of elders, and you are often drawn to structured faiths or long established schools of thought. Your beliefs are sensible and hard tested. Scepticism and caution can keep you from exploring anything that seems impractical. A journey taken purely for joy can surprise you with how much it teaches.",
    "aquarius": "You think for yourself, and your beliefs are often ahead of their time or quite unlike your upbringing. Conventional religion rarely fits; you gravitate to science, humanism, alternative philosophies, or a personal mix that makes sense to you alone. Travel appeals when it breaks your routine completely: an unusual destination, a gathering of like minded people, a sudden trip you decided on overnight. Learning thrives with freedom, and you often teach yourself online, far from the classroom. You are drawn to ideals that could improve the world for everyone. Your certainty about being progressive can make you surprisingly rigid, dismissing others as backward. Staying as curious about opposing views as about new ones keeps your thinking genuinely free.",
    "pisces": "Your sense of meaning is felt more than argued. You are drawn to mystical, spiritual and poetic ways of seeing the world, and a piece of music or a quiet chapel can teach you more than a textbook. Travel for you is dreamy and often life changing: a pilgrimage, a stay by the sea, a place you cannot stop thinking about years later. You learn best through imagination and stories, and you absorb a teacher's beliefs easily, sometimes too easily. Compassion is at the heart of your faith, and you are moved by other people's suffering wherever they live. Disillusionment has hit you hard when a guru or an ideal let you down. Your own inner guidance has proved more faithful than anyone else's vision."
  },
  "11": {
    "aries": "You make friends fast and lead them without trying. In any group you are the one who suggests the plan, starts the club or fires everyone up about a cause. Friendship with you is loyal and energetic; you will turn up at midnight if someone needs you, and you expect the same courage back. Your hopes for the future are bold, and you chase them with real drive, often long before anyone else sees the point. Networks grow around your enthusiasm. Tempers flare, though: you can fall out quickly over a competitive streak or a clash of egos, and some friendships burn bright and end suddenly. The groups that suit you best are the ones where you can start things and still have room to move.",
    "taurus": "Your friendships are few, steady and built to last. You would rather have a handful of people you have known for twenty years than a crowded contacts list, and you show loyalty through practical care: the good bottle of wine, the loan in a tight month, the lift to the airport. Groups draw you in when they share comforts, food, music, gardening, and you are the reliable member who keeps things going. Your hopes for the future are grounded in security: a home, savings, a life that feels abundant. You grow networks slowly, through trust. Resistance to change is the catch, and you can cling to an old circle long after it stops nourishing you, or turn away new people out of habit.",
    "gemini": "You know everyone: your phone is full of group chats, you connect a friend who needs a plumber with a friend who is one, and you move between very different circles with ease. Friendship for you runs on conversation, jokes and shared ideas, and you love a group with lively debate. Networks come naturally, and many opportunities in your life have arrived through a chance chat with an acquaintance. Your hopes for the future change often, as new interests pull you in several directions at once. You are a brilliant connector and carrier of news. The flip side is breadth over depth: you can have hundreds of friends and still feel that few of them really know you. Closeness grows with the ones who keep listening after the banter stops.",
    "cancer": "Your friends become family. You gather people around the kitchen table, remember birthdays, check in when someone has gone quiet, and turn a group into a place where people feel safe. You prefer a close, cosy circle to a vast network, and you are fiercely protective of the people inside it. Your hopes for the future centre on belonging: a home full of people, a community that looks after its own. You often end up as the parent figure of any group, whatever your age. Sensitivity makes group life tricky, since a small slight or being left out of a plan can wound you for weeks. When you feel secure among friends, you are one of the warmest, most loyal people anyone could know.",
    "leo": "You bring warmth and sparkle to every group you join. People gather around you naturally, and you are often the host, the organiser of the reunion or the friend whose birthday party everyone remembers. Friendship matters deeply to you, and you are generous, loyal and encouraging, the first to cheer when someone wins. Your hopes for the future are big and creative, and you want your life to mean something people will notice. Networks open for you through charisma and confidence. Hurt comes when the spotlight shifts: you feel it keenly when your contribution goes unrecognised or another friend takes centre stage. You thrive among people who celebrate you and whom you can proudly celebrate in return.",
    "virgo": "You are the friend who actually helps. You notice what someone needs, fix the spreadsheet for the committee, and quietly do the work that keeps a group running. Your friendships often grow from shared tasks: colleagues, volunteers, people on the same course. You prefer useful conversation to small talk, and you trust friends who are reliable more than friends who are merely fun. Your hopes for the future are practical: improving your skills, your health, your corner of the world, and networks grow through your competence. Criticism can creep in, though, whether you judge a group for being disorganised or feel you never contribute enough. Letting people help you as readily as you help them is what turns allies into close friends.",
    "libra": "You are sociable, gracious and good at bringing people together. In any group you are the peacemaker who notices who has been left out and smooths over tension before it becomes a row. Friendships matter as much as romance to you, and some of your closest friends started as partners or became partners. You love a gathering with beauty in it: a well laid table, good music, people who get on. Your hopes for the future centre on harmony and fairness, and causes about justice move you. The trouble is keeping everyone happy, which can leave your own opinion lost in the crowd. The friends who stay after you finally disagree with them are the true ones.",
    "scorpio": "You keep a small circle and guard it fiercely. Friendship with you is intense, discreet and deeply loyal, and the people you trust know they can tell you anything. You are wary of groups, sizing up who holds power and what everyone is hiding before you commit. Your hopes for the future are passionate, and you pursue them with a determination that surprises people. Networks for you run on quiet influence rather than numbers, and one powerful ally does more than a room of acquaintances. Betrayal by a friend cuts extremely deep, and you can end a friendship completely after one breach. Every circle you belong to changes you, and you come out of each one wiser about people.",
    "sagittarius": "Your friends come from everywhere: other countries, other faiths, other walks of life, and you love a group that widens your world. You are fun, generous and optimistic, the friend who proposes the road trip or the festival and makes it happen. Networks grow naturally around your enthusiasm, and doors open through people you met by chance while travelling or studying. Your hopes for the future are expansive, full of adventure, learning and freedom. You bring out the best in friends by believing in their dreams. Commitment is harder: you drift between circles and can forget the friend who needed you to stay. The friendships that last are the ones that let you roam and still welcome you home.",
    "capricorn": "You take friendship seriously and build it slowly. Your circle often includes older people, mentors, or colleagues who became friends through years of working side by side. You are the reliable one in a group, the treasurer, the person who remembers the deadline and turns a vague plan into a real one. Your hopes for the future are ambitious and long term, and you work steadily towards them, sometimes alone. Networks grow through reputation, and people respect your word. You can hold back emotionally in groups, feeling responsible rather than relaxed, and you leave the party early to get things done. Friendships often grow warmer as you age, and later life can bring you a circle richer than your youth ever did.",
    "aquarius": "Groups and friendship are where you shine. You are at ease among eccentrics, activists and misfits, and your friends are an unusual, varied crowd who share ideas rather than backgrounds. You care about the collective future, and a cause, a community project or an online network can matter to you as much as family. Your hopes are idealistic and often ahead of their time. You treat friends as equals and give them freedom. The difficulty is closeness: you can feel warmer towards humanity in general than to the one friend asking for your time tonight, and you pull away when a friendship turns clingy. Letting a few people in close gives you the belonging you have long offered everyone else.",
    "pisces": "Friendship for you is compassionate and slightly mystical. You meet kindred spirits in unexpected places, through music, art, spiritual groups or a charity, and you often sense instantly who belongs in your life. You give generously to friends, listening for hours, lending money, absorbing their sorrows. Groups can make you feel part of something larger, and you love a shared dream. Your hopes for the future are romantic and idealistic, and sometimes vague. Boundaries are the problem: you can be drawn in by people who take more than they give, or idealise a friend and feel betrayed when they turn out to be human. Your circle becomes healthier when you choose friends as carefully as you care for them."
  },
  "12": {
    "aries": "Your private battles are fought in silence. You carry an inner restlessness that others rarely see, and your anger can go underground, surfacing as a tension headache, a sleepless night or a sudden outburst that surprises even you. Solitude helps you most when it involves movement: a solitary run, a long swim, time alone to burn off what you cannot say. Dreams are often vivid and active, full of chases and fights. Hidden courage is one of your great strengths, and in a crisis you discover a boldness no one suspected. Underneath lurks a fear of being selfish or too much, so you stifle your own desires. Acting from the inside out, rather than hiding your fire, is your path to peace.",
    "taurus": "You need quiet comfort to recharge, and retreat for you means the garden, a warm bath, music, a sanctuary of beautiful objects. Your inner life is steadier than people realise, and you have hidden reserves of patience that carry you through long, lonely stretches. Fear often centres on security: waking at night worrying about money, or feeling that what you have could be taken away. You can hold onto old attachments unconsciously, keeping possessions or habits you no longer need. Spirituality speaks to you through nature and the body, walking in woods or sitting quietly on the grass. The pull towards comfort can turn into escapism, eating or spending to soothe a feeling. Trusting that you are safe without holding on so tight brings a deeper peace than any possession.",
    "gemini": "Your mind rarely stops, even in your sleep. You talk to yourself, write in private notebooks, and have conversations in your head that never get said aloud. Solitude restores you when it is filled with reading, journalling or quiet thinking, and you notice patterns in your dreams that intrigue you. Anxiety often lives here: overthinking at 3am, replaying an exchange, fearing you said the wrong thing. You have a hidden gift for understanding what others leave unsaid, and your intuition works through words and images. Secrets can build up, and you sometimes hide your real thoughts behind chatter. Your busy mind finds its spirit in stillness, the moment silence starts to feel like company rather than emptiness.",
    "cancer": "Your emotional life runs deep beneath the surface, and much of what you feel you keep hidden. Retreat means home, a quiet room, the sea, somewhere to cry without being watched. Old family feelings live in your unconscious and surface in dreams of houses, mothers and childhood rooms. You have a hidden capacity to care for people who are struggling, and you are often drawn to nursing, caring or quiet service. Many evenings you listen to a friend's heartache, then lie awake with it yourself. Fear of abandonment or of being a burden can make you swallow your needs, and moods arrive without explanation. Your inner child deserves the same gentleness you give everyone else, and receiving it heals you.",
    "leo": "You have more pride and hidden light than people see. In private you dream big, rehearse speeches, imagine a life that would make you proud, and yet you often hold back from claiming the spotlight in public. Solitude restores you when you create something just for yourself: painting, singing in the car, writing for no audience. A quiet fear of being unloved or ordinary sits underneath your warmth. You give generously behind the scenes, supporting others without credit, and your dreams are vivid and theatrical, full of performances and sunlit rooms. Unacknowledged needs for recognition can sour into secret resentment. Your worth shines without applause, and discovering that sets your inner light free.",
    "virgo": "Your inner world is busy with lists, worries and quiet self-criticism. Alone at night you replay mistakes and pick apart the day, and anxiety about health or doing things properly can hide beneath a calm exterior. Solitude works best when it is ordered: a tidy room, a routine of meditation, a slow walk, time to sort your thoughts. You have a hidden gift for service and healing, and you help others in unseen, practical ways, often without being thanked. Your dreams can be surprisingly detailed and symbolic. The fear of imperfection runs deep and can freeze you before you begin. Being enough as you are, with mercy extended to yourself, is the deepest peace this part of life holds.",
    "libra": "Your inner life longs for harmony, and you feel discord more than you show. In private you replay conflicts, imagine what you should have said, and worry about whether people truly like you. Solitude restores you when it is beautiful: music, art, a lovely room, time alone to reconnect with your own taste. There is a hidden strength in your sense of fairness, and you quietly work behind the scenes to bring peace. Relationships can carry secret elements, a hidden love or a longing never spoken. Fear of conflict or of being alone sits beneath much of what you do. Balance found inside yourself, rather than supplied by others, is the peace you have always been after.",
    "scorpio": "Your unconscious is deep and powerful, and you feel things at a level most people never reach. Much of your intensity stays hidden; you keep secrets, including some from yourself, and your dreams can be dark, vivid and revealing. Solitude is essential for you, a place to process and regenerate after the world has drained you. You have a hidden strength that emerges in crisis, a psychological resilience others underestimate. Fear of betrayal or loss of control lives beneath the surface and can drive compulsive habits. Therapy, research and spiritual practice suit you because you want the truth of your own depths. When you face what you have buried, you find extraordinary power to heal and transform.",
    "sagittarius": "You carry a quiet faith that something is looking out for you, and often it is. Even at your lowest you sense a hidden protection, and help keeps arriving from unexpected places: a stranger's kindness, a door that opens at the last minute. Solitude restores you through big thinking: reading philosophy, walking in open country, a solitary trip where you can breathe. Your dreams can be expansive, full of journeys and landscapes. Beneath your optimism lies a fear of being trapped or of life having no meaning. You can escape into restlessness, always planning the next adventure to avoid sitting with pain. Your search for truth, turned inward, finds its horizon in stillness.",
    "capricorn": "Beneath a composed surface you carry hidden responsibilities and fears. Alone, you worry about failure, about not doing enough, about being judged, and old feelings of having to grow up too soon can still shape you. Solitude helps you when it has structure: early mornings, quiet discipline, time to rebuild your strength. You have a hidden resilience that sees you through long hard stretches, and your dreams carry themes of tests, exams and climbing, the ambitions you rarely admit. A fear of dependence makes accepting help a struggle, even from people who love you. Spirituality for you is practical and earned, and it grows through commitment over years. Rest, you slowly learn, is not something you have to earn.",
    "aquarius": "Your inner life is unconventional and often surprising, with insights that arrive out of nowhere. In private you think about humanity, the future and ideas others would find strange, and you feel different from people even when you blend in. Solitude restores you when you can detach from the crowd and follow your own thoughts, and your dreams can be odd, futuristic or startlingly clear. You carry a hidden independence, and a fear of being trapped or ordinary sits beneath your friendliness. Emotions are often held at a distance, locked up until they erupt suddenly. Spirituality speaks to you through unusual paths: astrology, science, a group meditation, anything that feels liberating. Accepting your own difference without apology gives you the inner freedom you crave.",
    "pisces": "This is where you feel most at home, in the quiet, dreamy spaces most people avoid. Your imagination is vast, your dreams vivid and often meaningful, and you pick up on atmospheres and unspoken feelings instantly. Solitude is essential, whether by the sea, in music or in prayer, because the world easily overwhelms you. You have a deep hidden compassion and often feel called to help those who suffer quietly. Boundaries are hard, and you absorb other people's pain until you cannot tell which feelings are yours. The pull towards escape, through sleep, fantasy or a drink, can be strong. Spiritual life is where you thrive, and when you trust your intuition, it guides you with remarkable grace."
  }
};
